# The sdist ships the package, not the workbench.
#
# setuptools' default sdist picks up every .py file it finds, which pulled in
# tests/*.py but none of tests/conftest.py, tests/corpus/ or tests/snippets/ --
# an unrunnable suite, which is worse than no suite. Shipping the *whole* tree
# would not fix it either: tests/test_vocabulary_sync.py is marked `upstream`
# and fails rather than skips when pssparser's PSSLexer.g4 is absent, and it is
# absent in an sdist by design (the grammar is a development dependency; see
# DESIGN.md section 4.4).
#
# So the test suite stays a repository artifact. Verification of a release
# happens in CI against the built wheel, which is where the corpus and the
# grammar both exist.
prune tests
prune scripts
prune docs
prune packages
exclude cspell.json
exclude ivpm.yaml
exclude DESIGN.md
